{#
  Which SASL login may use which envelope sender, for
  smtpd_sender_login_maps in main.cf. Before this map existed,
  `permit_sasl_authenticated` came first in smtpd_sender_restrictions,
  so any logged-in account could send as any address at all - and
  since RSpamd signs authenticated mail for every served domain, a
  stolen password produced correctly DKIM-signed mail from any address
  here. With `reject_authenticated_sender_login_mismatch` now ahead of
  that permit, an authenticated sender address that is missing from
  this map, or owned by another login, is refused with `553 5.7.1`.
  That includes every address outside the served domains.

  Ownership, for each served domain:

    - <account>@<domain> belongs to the account. Logins are bare names,
      because Dovecot's `auth_username_format = %n` drops any domain the
      client sends and hands Postfix the result. That is the
      sasl_username Postfix logs, and the only form this map needs.

    - <alias>@<domain> belongs to every account the alias delivers to,
      following alias chains to the end: `postmaster -> root -> <user>`
      gives postmaster@ to <user>. That matches valiases.j2, which
      resolves the same names the same way. Somebody who receives an
      address's mail may also send as it, and nobody else may.

  An alias that leads to no account (e.g. one that forwards only to
  root, when root is itself unaliased) gets no line. Nobody can send as
  it, because nobody receives its mail as a login.

  The chain walk is bounded by the number of aliases, which is the
  longest chain possible without a cycle; `seen` stops a cycle early.
#}
# Envelope sender -> SASL logins allowed to use it
{% set alias_targets = {} %}
{% for entry in mail.aliases %}
{%   set _ = alias_targets.update({entry.alias: entry.forwards}) %}
{% endfor %}
{% set accounts = users.users | map(attribute='name') | list %}
{% set owners = {} %}
{% for name in (accounts + (alias_targets | list)) | unique %}
{%   set walk = namespace(frontier=[name], seen=[], found=[]) %}
{%   for _ in range((alias_targets | length) + 1) %}
{%     set step = namespace(next=[]) %}
{%     for n in walk.frontier | unique if n not in walk.seen %}
{%       set _ = walk.seen.append(n) %}
{%       if n in accounts %}
{%         set _ = walk.found.append(n) %}
{%       endif %}
{%       set step.next = step.next + alias_targets.get(n, []) %}
{%     endfor %}
{%     set walk.frontier = step.next %}
{%   endfor %}
{%   if walk.found %}
{%     set _ = owners.update({name: walk.found | unique | sort}) %}
{%   endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% for d in [domain] + domain_aliases %}
{%   for name in owners | sort %}
{{ name }}@{{ d }} {{ owners[name] | join(', ') }}
{%   endfor %}
{% endfor %}
